-- title:
--   Cusp zero-chart dictionary under a small opposite coordinate
-- statement:
--   Fix a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$ and a nonzero level $N$ with $\ell \nmid N$, modular polynomial data `data` at level $\ell$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence (the reduction of its bivariate polynomial $\Phi$ modulo $\ell$ equals $(C(X)^{\ell}-X)(C(X)-X^{\ell})$), a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$, together with the integrality of the two degeneracy embeddings $\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}$ and $\mathrm{heckeBetaBar}$ from the base-changed level-$N$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to level $N\ell$, modular polynomial data `dataAll d` for every divisor $d \mid N$, the evaluation-symmetry of $\Phi_N$ on Laurent series, the separability of $\Phi_N$ over $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$ after reduction mod $\ell$, a fibre model `fm` of level $N$ over $A$ with reduction $\mathrm{red}$ (subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the base-changed function field, integral over the affine bases generated by the $A$-constants and $\bar j$ respectively $\bar j^{-1}$, with reduction homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}},\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ matching constants, $\bar j$ and $\bar j_N$), and a cusp chart `cc` for it (so $\bar j_N \bar j^{-N} \in B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ with the expected image under $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$). Here $\bar j$ and $\bar j_N$ denote the images of $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,N$. Then for every place $w$ of that field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $\tau \in A$, and every witness that $t := \bar j/\bar j_N^{\,N}$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$: if $w.\mathrm{ord}(\bar j_N - a) \le 0$ for all $a \in A$, if the residue of $t$ at $w$ is the image of $\tau$ in the residue field of $w$, and if $\bar j_N/\bar j^{\,N} - a$ is a nonunit of the valuation subring of $w$ for some $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, then, with $t_k := j_k/j_{N,k}^{\,N}$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$, either $t_k - \mathrm{red}(\tau) = 0$ or its order at the place $(\mathrm{fm.spPlace}\,\mathrm{hred}\,\mathrm{dataAll}\,\mathrm{hsep})(w)$ is strictly positive.
--
--   This is one configuration of the specialisation dictionary at a cusp in the zero-chart of the coordinate $t = \bar j/\bar j_N^{\,N}$: the case in which the opposite coordinate $\bar j_N/\bar j^{\,N}$ is congruent to an element of the maximal ideal of $A$ modulo the nonunits of $w$, which forces the reduced coordinate $t_k$ either to vanish identically or to vanish at the specialised place. It feeds the corresponding dictionary statement [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d7_dictZero_of_t_small`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d7_dictZero_of_t_small).
